# Aji Verde

Source: The Daring Gourmet, "Aji Verde (Peruvian Green Sauce)" by Kimberly Killebrew. https://www.daringgourmet.com/peruvian-aji-verde-sauce/

## Recipe Name: Aji Verde (Peruvian Green Sauce)

## Servings: 6 (serving size 2 tablespoons; makes about 3/4 cup)

## Prep Time: 5 mins

## Cook Time: None

## Ingredients:
### Sauce:
- 2 green jalapeño peppers, seeded
- 2 cups loosely packed fresh cilantro leaves
- 1 small clove garlic
- 1 green onion, chopped
- 2 teaspoons huacatay paste
- 1 tablespoon aji amarillo paste
- 1 tablespoon fresh lime juice
- 1 tablespoon extra virgin olive oil
- 1/4 cup Cotija, queso fresco, or Parmesan cheese
- 1/4 teaspoon salt
- 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper
- 1/2 cup good quality mayonnaise

## Instructions:
### Blend the Sauce:
1. Put all ingredients in a food processor or blender.
2. Blend until the sauce is a smooth paste. Scrape down the sides if the cilantro stays chunky.

### Store:
1. Put the sauce in an airtight container and refrigerate.
2. Use the sauce within one week.

